  "details": "Right now it seems that the VRC_VideoSync script has no option for watching un-synced and triggering it to enable/disable locally. \n\nI've done some pretty extensive playing around with the player and I'm pretty sure that this can't be done currently; at least not in any way that I've tried so far.  If it's indeed possible, I'd love to hear a confirmed method. \n\nExample usage: \nAdd options for background music in a room; each player can enable/disable the music and select a song to listen to.\n\nPeople get around this limitation by uploading audio files to their world, which tends to inflate world download size.\n\nAdding an option to have an unsynced video player should save some disk space/download size on worlds, plus give developers more options when adding audio to their world.",
